# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party guidance, standards and reports: never committed.
#
# Per the repo-root convention, copyrighted PDFs are not redistributed here;
# 04.references/README.md records provenance and retrieval for each. As of
# 2026-08-01 `standards/` alone is 1.5 GB and contains a 351 MB archive and a
# 137 MB raster, both far over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
#
# The markdown conversions under standards/ are excluded too: they are the text
# of copyrighted guidance, and converting a format does not change that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
04.references/reports/
04.references/standards/
04.references/ipcc-guidelines/

# macOS resource forks
._*
.DS_Store
.Rproj.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw input data: NEVER committed.
#
# Per the repo-root convention, large third-party data lives on the external
# drive and git carries only a manifest of provenance plus the small derived
# CSVs the manuscript actually cites. As of 2026-07-30 this tree holds 2.7 GB,
# including single files of 1.2 GB, 731 MB and 265 MB. GitHub hard-rejects any
# file over 100 MB, so an accidental `git add 02.inputs` would wedge the repo.
#
# Everything under 02.inputs is ignored by default; the exceptions below
# re-admit the documentation and the derived outputs, which are small and are
# what the paper reads.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
02.inputs/**
!02.inputs/
!02.inputs/**/
!02.inputs/**/*.md
!02.inputs/**/*.R
!02.inputs/**/*.py
!02.inputs/derived/**

# Derived CSVs written by the pre-processing scripts ARE committed: they are
# the numbers the manuscript cites, and the rule is that no figure may be
# quoted from code that was not saved.
!02.inputs/derived/*.csv

# The derived/** re-admission above would otherwise let macOS resource forks
# back in; re-exclude them last so the ._* rule wins.
02.inputs/**/._*
**/._*

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Quarto render sidecar: 31 MB of regenerable JS/CSS libraries.
01.manuscript/*_files/
